  "답변 내용(영문)": {
   "null_rate": 0.0,
   "unique": 23,
   "top": {
    "To utilize an open API, you must first submit an application for use to the relevant API provider. Search for the desired open API on the public data portal, click the [Apply for Use] button on the details page, and enter the purpose of use and authentication type to complete the application. Applications for use are divided into automatic approval and deliberation approval, which can be distinguished through the [Deliberation Type] item on the API details page. APIs subject to deliberation approval are approved after review by the provider, and once approval is complete, you can check the status and service key in &#39;My Page > Data Utilization > Open API > Application for Use Status&#39;. The issued service key can be used for all open APIs as one key, and if you already have a key, you do not need to issue a new one. However, if you reissue a service key, the existing key will be automatically deleted, so be sure to replace it with a new key. Service keys are issued per user, and only one key can be operated per person.": 1,
    "In the Public Data Portal, only one service key is issued per member account, and one service key can be used for all open APIs. If you apply for a new key while holding an existing key, the existing key will be automatically canceled, so please be sure to change to a new key to avoid interruption of existing services.": 1,
    "The use guarantee means that users can freely process and use the data to the extent that they maintain the factual content of public data provided by public institutions. no. If a user violates the use requirements of public data or abuses illegal activities such as crime, the public institution may take measures such as suspension of provision and imposition of a fine.": 1,
    "It is necessary to examine whether the requested public data is excluded from the provision, and to notify the applicant by deciding whether to provide it within 10 days (excluding holidays) from the day the request is received. If it is not possible to decide whether to provide within the specified period, the period for determining whether to provide can be extended within a range of 10 days (excluding holidays), and the applicant must be notified of the extended facts and reasons without delay. ※ If the decision to reject the offer is made, the public institution must include the following phrase in the official notice when notifying the applicant of the content and reason of the decision to reject. If there is an objection to the decision of the public institution to refuse to provide public data, within 60 days from the date of receiving the notice of the decision to refuse to provide the public in accordance with Article 27, Paragraph 5 of the 「Act on the Promotion and Use of Public Data」 You can file a dispute resolution on the rejection of the provision with the Public Data Provision Dispute Mediation Committee under Article 31 (1).": 1,
    "In accordance with the&#39;Public Organization Database Standardization Guidelines&#39;, public institutions must perform the following tasks to standardize the public database. 1. Establishment of standardization management system 2. Establishment and application management of public database standards 3. Inspection and improvement of standardization 4. Management and management of institutional meta-systems such as registration and implementation of meta data 5. Management of standard terminology and application of common standard terms 6 Compliance management of open standards 7. Other matters specified by the Minister of Public Administration and Security regarding standardization": 1,
    "In the case of building a system through the introduction of a package or a solution, it is necessary to define a list of deliverables that must be completed from the data quality point of view, and to manage and supervise the related deliverables through a contractor.": 1,
